# SemanticScript standard-library canonical module: standard.bit.

module standard.bit
purpose module standard.bit "Canonical standard-library module for bit operations."
moduleOwns standard.bit "The official import path `standard.bit` and this module's implementation body."
moduleDoesNotOwn standard.bit "App-specific wrappers, compatibility aliases, or generated build artifacts."
invariant module standard.bit "The standard module entry is this file; tests live beside it as `main.test.sem`."

exportConstant standard.bit bitModuleVersionText
storage module immutable bitModuleVersionText CNullTerminatedByteString "standard.bit 0.1"

# Canonical standard-library implementation body.
# ============================================================
# SEMANTICSCRIPT STANDARD LIBRARY: bitwise operations on CSignedInt64
# ============================================================
#
# rationale: SemanticScript's math.* surface has no native bitwise
#   primitives (and/or/xor/not/shift), so this module implements
#   them via multiplication, division, and modulo. Each bit op is
#   pure-SemanticScript â€” no libc, no special LLVM intrinsics â€” and constant-
#   folds when both operands are compile-time constants.
#
# invariant: shifts are unsigned-equivalent (multiplication /
#   division by 2^k). isSignedInt64BitSet checks the k-th bit of
#   the abstract base-2 representation, equivalent to ((n >> k) & 1).
#   setSignedInt64Bit / clearSignedInt64Bit / toggleSignedInt64Bit
#   preserve every other bit.
#
# security: pure value-level math; no allocation; no branches
#   over secret-dependent bit patterns beyond the standard k-step
#   power-of-two loop.
#
# timing: O(k) where k is bitIndex (loop bound). Acceptable for
#   bitIndex up to 63; not for hot inner loops. Future revisions
#   should expose LLVM `shl`/`lshr`/`and`/`or`/`xor` intrinsics.
#
# observability: no logs, no metrics.
#
# warning: bitIndex must be in [0, 63]. Values outside this
#   range silently wrap (multiplication by 2^64 overflows back).
#
# Operations exposed:
#   shiftSignedInt64BitsLeft(inputValue, bitIndex)   -> CSignedInt64
#   shiftSignedInt64BitsRight(inputValue, bitIndex)  -> CSignedInt64
#   isSignedInt64BitSet(inputValue, bitIndex)        -> Bool
#   setSignedInt64Bit(inputValue, bitIndex)          -> CSignedInt64
#   clearSignedInt64Bit(inputValue, bitIndex)        -> CSignedInt64
#   toggleSignedInt64Bit(inputValue, bitIndex)       -> CSignedInt64

# This is a pure-module (library) file: it exports operations
# consumed by other programs (notably std/bit/main.test.sem which
# importModules it and runs the smoke). The project / target /
# runtime / entry block is retained so the module can still be
# linted standalone â€” the entry just points at the first exported
# operation rather than a `main` smoke.

domainLiteral integerZeroComparisonValue CSignedInt64 0
domainLiteralTrust integerZeroComparisonValue trustedStaticLiteral
domainLiteral integerOneStepValue CSignedInt64 1
domainLiteralTrust integerOneStepValue trustedStaticLiteral
domainLiteral integerTwoBaseValue CSignedInt64 2
domainLiteralTrust integerTwoBaseValue trustedStaticLiteral

# section bit.shift

operation shiftSignedInt64BitsLeft
input operation shiftSignedInt64BitsLeft inputValue CSignedInt64
input operation shiftSignedInt64BitsLeft bitIndex CSignedInt64
output operation shiftSignedInt64BitsLeft CSignedInt64
memory shiftSignedInt64BitsLeft heap no
async shiftSignedInt64BitsLeft no
purpose operation shiftSignedInt64BitsLeft "Returns inputValue << bitIndex, computed as inputValue * 2^bitIndex."
invariant operation shiftSignedInt64BitsLeft "For bitIndex in [0, 63] and non-overflowing values, equivalent to LLVM's shl."
warning shiftSignedInt64BitsLeft "Overflow wraps modulo 2^64; bitIndex < 0 is undefined."
guarantee shiftSignedInt64BitsLeft "Terminates after bitIndex iterations."
label startShiftSignedInt64BitsLeft
memory shiftSignedInt64BitsLeft mutable leftShiftPowerAccumulator I64 1
memory shiftSignedInt64BitsLeft mutable leftShiftIteration I64 0
label leftShiftLoop
call detectLeftShiftDoneCall math.greaterThanOrEqualI64
argument detectLeftShiftDoneCall left I64 leftShiftIteration
argument detectLeftShiftDoneCall right I64 bitIndex
run detectLeftShiftDoneCall
bind value leftShiftDone Bool detectLeftShiftDoneCall
branch if condition leftShiftDone target applyLeftShiftMultiplication
call doubleLeftShiftPowerCall math.multiplyI64
argument doubleLeftShiftPowerCall left I64 leftShiftPowerAccumulator
argument doubleLeftShiftPowerCall right I64 integerTwoBaseValue
run doubleLeftShiftPowerCall
bind value doubledLeftShiftPower I64 doubleLeftShiftPowerCall
set memory leftShiftPowerAccumulator doubledLeftShiftPower
call incrementLeftShiftIterationCall math.addI64
argument incrementLeftShiftIterationCall left I64 leftShiftIteration
argument incrementLeftShiftIterationCall right I64 integerOneStepValue
run incrementLeftShiftIterationCall
bind value nextLeftShiftIteration I64 incrementLeftShiftIterationCall
set memory leftShiftIteration nextLeftShiftIteration
jump target leftShiftLoop
label applyLeftShiftMultiplication
call multiplyInputByPowerCall math.multiplyI64
argument multiplyInputByPowerCall left I64 inputValue
argument multiplyInputByPowerCall right I64 leftShiftPowerAccumulator
run multiplyInputByPowerCall
bind value shiftedLeftResult CSignedInt64 multiplyInputByPowerCall
return value shiftedLeftResult

operation shiftSignedInt64BitsRight
input operation shiftSignedInt64BitsRight inputValue CSignedInt64
input operation shiftSignedInt64BitsRight bitIndex CSignedInt64
output operation shiftSignedInt64BitsRight CSignedInt64
memory shiftSignedInt64BitsRight heap no
async shiftSignedInt64BitsRight no
purpose operation shiftSignedInt64BitsRight "Returns inputValue >> bitIndex, computed as inputValue / 2^bitIndex (arithmetic for signed values via LLVM sdiv)."
